        "math_academy_id": "q-90319",
        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/387709ca72b5591528b5f5ac95886f0dab331ef2cb67955803e7a252cecef966.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?",
        "worked_solution": "Consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=2x+3.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le 2x+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines our shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y\\le 2x+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
